  "term": "instrumental activities of daily living",
  "definition": "Instrumental activities of daily living are the more complex everyday tasks needed for independent living in the community, such as shopping, cooking, commuting, and managing household affairs. Compared with basic self-care activities, they place greater demands on memory, attention, executive abilities, and physical functioning.",
